      "text": "right. UNESCO reminds us that access to official information empowers citizens to participate meaningfully in democratic life. For this reason, the United Nations proclaims 28 September as the International Day for Universal Access to Official Information, recognizing its vital role. Each year, this day brings governments, civil societies and citizens together to reflect on progress and recommit to ensuring that the right to know is respected everywhere. The Council of Europe Convention on Access to Official Documents, the Tromsa Convention, becomes the first binding international treaty to guarantee the right of everyone to access official information. Entering into force in 2020, it affirms that transparency is a democratic obligation and this right should be guaranteed without discrimination. Across Europe, most countries",
