      "text": "have adopted national freedom of information laws. At the European Union level, access to official information is governed by this special regulation. And in addition, there are open data directives, which set minimum standards for making public sector digital data accessible and reusable. Together, these frameworks create a strong foundation, but they also highlight practical challenges, delays, big projective disclosure and limited events. Let's have a look at the Tromsa Convention and how it ensures access to digital data. Article 1 of the Tromsa Convention defines official documents as all information recorded in any form, drawn up or received and held by public authorities. Article 9 goes further, requiring state parties to take measures to ensure that the information is managed efficiently, though it is easily accessible",
